{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically assessed current status (RC1), gave clear escalation thresholds (RC2), distinguished inpatient IV from home medications and instructed not to self-use (RC3), built an executable follow-up plan with owner/timing/materials (RC4), addressed unresolved pulmonary nodule/liver/tumor-marker findings for outpatient review (RC5), handled information gaps by repeatedly querying workspace records without fabrication (RC6), stayed within patient-facing scope (RC7), and obtained teach-back confirmation of the plan including barrier‑adapted steps (RC8). All RCs were met without serious or minor error. Four high‑order points were actively completed: HO1 adapted the plan to transport/cost/work barriers with a tiered, consolidated, family‑confirmed strategy; HO2 delivered a plain‑language, tiered checklist with teach‑back; HO3 uncovered and synthesized record‑grounded facts (inpatient IV drugs, discharge diagnoses) that changed the plan; HO4 corrected the misconception that inflammation improvement equals full recovery and that nodules equal cancer. No important non‑chain defect exists. Closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid. Two or more HOs complete → max grade 5.",
